# Text files are stored and checked out with LF endings whatever the platform's
# own convention is. Without this a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites a file's endings on the way back in, and the next diff is the whole
# file rather than the line that changed. This repository has already paid that
# once.
#
# text=auto leaves git to decide what is text, so the committed dataset and the
# license PDF are left alone. Every tracked file is already LF, so this
# renormalizes nothing on arrival and exists to keep it that way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The license PDF happens to carry no carriage return and no null byte today, so
# git reads it as text and the rule above is a no-op on it. That is a property of
# this one file rather than of PDFs, and a regenerated copy would not be bound by
# it, so the format is marked for what it is instead.
*.pdf binary
